file
Usage: file [-k] PATH

Identifies what a blob actually is by reading its bytes, not trusting its name
or extension. The first question to ask of anything unknown: an ELF binary, a
gzip stream, a jpeg, plain text? `file` answers before you open it.

	file PATH     name the type from the content
	-k            keep going -- show every type it matches, not just the first

See also: binwalk, strace, radare2
